# Generated by the capture pipeline. Everything here is reproducible from the
# committed raw frames plus lines.md, and some of it is large.
#
# What IS committed, deliberately: episodes/*/frames/raw and frames/clean.
# Those are the only irreplaceable part -- re-capturing them means driving a
# real mailbox again, while a wording change is only a re-render. Three wording
# changes landed as free re-renders because 004's frames were in the repo; 003
# could not take them because its frames were swept.
#
# Comments go on their own line. A trailing "# ..." is part of the pattern, not
# a comment, so a rule written that way silently matches nothing -- which is how
# the first version of this file let 21 mp3s and a 1.4 MB intermediate into the
# index.

# edge-tts output, regenerated by every render
episodes/*/frames/voice/

# stills pulled to proofread a cut
episodes/*/frames/review/

# absolute paths, machine-specific
episodes/*/frames/concat.txt
episodes/*/frames/picture_len

# pre-overlay intermediate
episodes/*/frames/raw-*.mp4
episodes/*/frames/render.log

# scratch grabs taken while aiming a shot
episodes/*/frames/_*.png
